                    insight_orchestrated:   `Orchestrated studio: distinctiveness at or above baseline, shipped on time and on budget with no legal flag, and analytics-sharpened engagement. You amplified creativity with AI instead of flattening it — and answered the board's question.`,
                    insight_forgettable:    `On time, forgettable: you hit the shelf and the budget but distinctiveness came in flat, indistinguishable from last year. Against an insurgent eating six share points, speed without distinctiveness is just efficient mediocrity.`,
                    insight_late:           `You missed the fixed retail launch date. Beautiful work that ships after the shelf reset arrives to an empty calendar slot — the throughput generative AI offered on variants and localisation was the way to hit the date without touching the core.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed launch. Re-read where you placed generative versus non-generative AI: the gains live in scaling production and sharpening targeting, the losses in letting the machine near the creative core.`,
                    insight_legal:          `A legal flag is live: a generated asset raised a rights/likeness/disclosure problem with no gate to catch it. During a defining relaunch this becomes the headline instead of the product.`,
                    insight_overbudget:     `You ran over the €1.8M budget — the all-human-style path costs around €2.4M and misses the date. AI throughput on production tasks is how the maths closes.`,
                    insight_above:          `Distinctiveness pushed well above baseline — the relaunch is being noticed and remembered as Aurore, not regressed to the category mean. That is what defends the line.`,
                    insight_engage:         `Strong six-channel engagement — your non-generative analytics sharpened targeting without ever touching a creative asset, exactly the role that tooling should play.`,

                    hint_legal:             `A rights/likeness/disclosure flag is live. Place a review gate on generated assets before print, and disclose AI use — governance is part of the workflow, not an afterthought.`,
                    hint_flat:              `Distinctiveness has dropped below baseline — the machine is regressing your brand to the mean. Pull generative AI off the creative core and put humans (or co-creation) back on concept and voice.`,
                    hint_late:              `You are tracking past the five-week retail date. Let generative AI absorb variant production and localisation — that is the throughput that hits the date without touching the concept.`,
                    hint_budget:            `You are over the €1.8M budget. The all-human path costs around €2.4M; aim generative throughput at production tasks to bring the cost back inside the cap.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — distinctiveness at or above baseline, on the date, no legal flag. Lock in per-task calibration and an honest disclosure to defend the studio's AI mandate.`,

